{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":58233,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fbec7290-abe9-545e-84d9-f4ba00463aa9","total_cost_usd":0.5302459999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12332,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5514,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12332,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5514,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12332},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7811,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.007886,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5514,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12332,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5223599999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:dependence-free-batch-b-reviewer-fable-18\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:6a3bc02816cb70ee4042\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The data description designates the well as the independent unit and states that the six rounds per well are repeated, non-independent measurements that should be reduced to one value per well before comparison.\", \"observed_value\": \"Independent unit column: well_id; 18 wells x 6 rounds = 108 rows\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 14, \"quoted_text\": \"One row is: one water sample drawn from one monitoring well on one survey round\\nIndependent unit column: well_id\"}, {\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 16, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"The eighteen wells are the independent units of the study. The six rounds\\nrecorded for a given well are repeated measurements of the same piece of aquifer\\nand are not independent of one another, so an analysis that reports a claim about\\nthe restoration should reduce each well to a single value\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow collapses each well's repeated rounds to a single baseline-to-post change score before any inference, so each independent unit enters the tested dataset exactly once.\", \"observed_value\": \"collapse_to_wells produces one change score per well_id (18 scores)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 36, \"end_line\": 43, \"quoted_text\": \"def collapse_to_wells(readings):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One paired change score per well: post-period mean minus baseline mean.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    contrasts = []\\n    for well in sorted(readings):\\n        baseline = readings[well][BASELINE_LABEL]\\n        post = readings[well][POST_LABEL]\\n        baseline_mean = statistics.fmean(baseline)\\n        post_mean = statistics.fmean(post)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The statistical test is an exact binomial sign test applied to the signs of the 18 well-level change scores, not to the 108 sample-level rows.\", \"observed_value\": \"binomtest(n_down=15, n_tested=18, 0.5, two-sided)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 70, \"end_line\": 76, \"quoted_text\": \"    signed = [value for value in changes if value != 0.0]\\n    n_tested = len(signed)\\n    n_down = sum(1 for value in signed if value < 0.0)\\n    n_up = n_tested - n_down\\n    n_flat = n_wells - n_tested\\n\\n    outcome = binomtest(n_down, n_tested, 0.5, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\")\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The reported selected result claims n = 18 independent well-level change scores with p = 0.007538; independent recomputation of the exact two-sided binomial test for 15 of 18 declines gives 2 x (816+153+18+1)/2^18 = 1976/262144 = 0.007538, confirming the p-value was computed on well-level units, not rows.\", \"observed_value\": \"recomputed p = 0.0075378... matches reported p = 0.007538\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 42, \"end_line\": 42, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial sign test on 18 independent well-level change scores: 15/18 wells declined (estimated proportion 0.833), p = 0.007538; median well-level change -1.10 mg/L.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The well-level change scores in the report table are correctly derived from the raw rows; e.g., W-01 baseline rows (11.2, 10.6, 11.5) mean 11.10 and post rows (9.4, 8.8, 9.7) mean 9.30 give the tabulated change of -1.80, and the direction counts (15 decreases, 3 increases: W-05, W-12, W-16) match the raw data.\", \"observed_value\": \"W-01 change -1.80; 15 down / 3 up / 0 tied across 18 wells\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 17, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"| W-01 | 3 / 3 | 11.10 | 9.30 | -1.80 | decrease |\"}, {\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"W-01,6.5,baseline,R1,12,11.2\"}, {\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 56, \"end_line\": 56, \"quoted_text\": \"W-01,6.5,post_restoration,R4,215,9.4\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 40, \"end_line\": 40, \"quoted_text\": \"15 of the 18 wells (83.3%) had a lower mean nitrate concentration after reconnection, 3 had a higher mean, and 0 were unchanged.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The input file does contain six rows per independent unit (e.g., well W-01 appears on six data rows), so repeated entries of each well into the raw table exist and could have fed a row-independent procedure had the workflow skipped aggregation; the code, however, aggregates these rows within read_long_table/collapse_to_wells before testing, so this repetition never reaches the inference.\", \"observed_value\": \"6 rows per well_id in data/input.csv; aggregated before binomtest\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"W-01,6.5,baseline,R1,12,11.2\"}, {\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 20, \"end_line\": 20, \"quoted_text\": \"W-01,6.5,baseline,R2,40,10.6\"}, {\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 92, \"end_line\": 92, \"quoted_text\": \"W-01,6.5,post_restoration,R6,271,9.7\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 46, \"end_line\": 46, \"quoted_text\": \"The test treats wells, not individual water samples, as replicates. Pooling all 108 sample-level records into a sample-by-sample comparison would count every well 6 times and would overstate the evidence; the reported p-value rests on the 18 well-level scores alone.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to show that the reported p-value could only have come from entering wells repeatedly into a row-independent test. I recomputed the exact two-sided binomial sign test on the 18 well-level signs derived independently from the raw rows: 15 of 18 wells declined, giving p = 2 x (C(18,15)+C(18,16)+C(18,17)+C(18,18))/2^18 = 1976/262144 = 0.007538, which matches the reported p exactly. A row-level version of the analysis would have used n = 108 samples or n = 54 round-level pairs, which cannot reproduce p = 0.007538 with 15/18 declines. I also traced the code path: binomtest receives n_down and n_tested computed from the per-well change scores produced by collapse_to_wells, with no branch that passes sample-level rows into the test, and spot-checked three wells' means and signs against the CSV (all consistent). The falsification failed on every check, so the issue class is not demonstrated.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":32338,"ttft_stream_ms":2318,"time_to_request_ms":17,"type":"result","duration_ms":58941,"uuid":"bc3bed97-f944-4d7a-a336-73d7637cba95"}
